# Netlify / Cloudflare Pages equivalent of the "headers" block in vercel.json.
# Each host reads only its own file, so both can sit here harmlessly.
# Keep the two in sync if you change anything below.
#
# NOTE: there is deliberately no _redirects file in this repo. The domain root
# is the faero OS desktop (index.html), which every host serves at "/" without
# help. The social app is a window inside that OS and is also reachable directly at
# /faero_v1_launch.html. An earlier copy of this config came from the
# standalone-app repo and rewrote "/" to the social app — that would have
# replaced the desktop with the app.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self'
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(), interest-cohort=()

# SAMEORIGIN / 'self' rather than DENY / 'none' on purpose: the OS frames the
# social app same-origin, and DENY blocks that too. SAMEORIGIN still stops
# third-party clickjacking.
#
# camera and microphone are intentionally NOT locked down — the Disposable
# and Calendar/stampcam apps use getUserMedia, and the OS grants them via the
# iframe allow= attribute. Blocking them here would kill both apps.

/faero_v1_launch.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate

/
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate

/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate
